<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.1.1: Understanding Exponents</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01235</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.1.1: Understanding Exponents</md:title>
    <md:uuid>68390a7f-20ff-4b8b-a700-01e5313fd0e8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>An exponent indicates repeated multiplication of the same quantity.</para>
<image alt="First example: a raised to the power of m equals a times a times a times a and so on until you have multiplied m different factors of a together. Second example: the quantity negative 9 raised to the power of 5 equals negative 9 times negative 9 times negative 9 times negative 9 times negative 9, a total of 5 factors of negative 9." class="img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="101" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/52807ddc47e36cc0c088995b28577d0de4058c58" width="550"/><para>Expand each exponential expression to show repeated multiplication.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(4^3\)= ____________</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(4 \cdot 4 \cdot 4\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(x^5\)= ____________</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(x \cdot x \cdot x \cdot x \cdot x\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\((-8)^6\) = ____________</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\((-8) \cdot (-8) \cdot (-8) \cdot (-8) \cdot (-8) \cdot (-8)\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\((-z)^3\) = ____________</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\((-z) \cdot (-z) \cdot (-z)\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
</content>
